<p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> Algae is not the end of your hydroponic garden. It's a fixable problem. Catch it early with pH monitoring. Treat it with hydrogen peroxide. Prevent it by blocking light. I ignored mine for 2 weeks and almost lost everything. Don't make the same mistake. <a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Hydrogen+Peroxide+3+percent+USP&tag=tabletopharve-20" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored">Grab a bottle of hydrogen peroxide on Amazon</a>. It was about $3 when I bought mine. If you see even a hint of green, use it. Your plants will thank you.</p>

